    <string name="launcher_empty_title">Getting started</string>
    <string name="launcher_empty_guide">To start playing, create an instance — an installed copy of Against the Storm. Pack the game\'s Windows version into a ZIP (the folder with \"Against the Storm.exe\") and add it with the + at the top.</string>
    <!-- "What's new" dialog, shown once per version (LauncherFragment.maybeShowReleaseNotes). English
         only, like the release notes it is cut from. Read with getText, so <b>/<i> are kept; keep it on
         one line, because a line break inside a string resource turns into a leading space. -->
    <string name="release_notes_title">What\'s new in v%1$s</string>
    <string name="release_notes_body"><b>– Mali GPUs</b>\nTheir drivers lack the texture format the PC game ships in, so textures are now converted while loading.\n\n<b>– Graphics profiles</b>\nLow and Very low in the instance settings. Very low turns the effects off for weak GPUs. New installs start on Low, or on Very low on GPUs without PC texture support. Pressing a button again resets the game to that profile.\n\n<b>– Cursor fix</b>\nIn the 1366×768 mode with black margins the cursor drifted away from your finger. Fixed.\n\n<b>– Steam download fix</b>\nPacking the downloaded game into a zip could fail with \"FileNotFoundException\". Fixed.\n\n<b>– Faster Steam download</b>\nTwelve connections now fetch the game\'s data, so big files no longer download one piece at a time.\n\n<b>– Better bug reports</b>\nThe report now shows FPS, frame times, CPU load, memory, GPU details and the game\'s graphics settings, so we can see what slows your game down.</string>
